          "line": 26,
          "message": "The JWT matcher excludes valid three-part base64url tokens whose encoded header starts with a character other than e or w, allowing them through telemetry (OWASP A09:2025).",
          "confidence": 0.87,
          "category": "security",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "Log properties, scopes, and trace attributes pass strings through ScrubText, which applies Jwt(). That regex only matches tokens whose first base64url segment starts with e or w.",
            "failureScenario": "A caller logs a valid compact JWT whose JSON header starts with whitespace, such as `IHsiYWxnIjoiSFMyNTYifQ.e30.c2ln`, under an ordinary property name. Its first segment starts with I, so Jwt() does not match and the token reaches the provider or exporter unchanged. This violates the specified three-part JWT redaction shape (OWASP A09:2025)."
          }
        }
